WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.042
“Renewals”

2
00:00:01.042 --> 00:00:02.759
shows renewals by urgency:

3
00:00:02.946 --> 00:00:06.916
expired, today, in seven, fifteen or thirty days.

4
00:00:07.381 --> 00:00:10.120
You can include life anniversaries too.

5
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.462
The “Next best action”

6
00:00:12.462 --> 00:00:16.294
card, here and on the Now screen, shows for each renewal

7
00:00:16.294 --> 00:00:20.658
of the next sixty days the move worth making now, with the reason:

8
00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.515
first the overdue premium, a call before any

9
00:00:23.515 --> 00:00:25.836
offer if the client gave a low score,

10
00:00:26.081 --> 00:00:29.818
a check of the rebuild value, or asking for renewal terms.

11
00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.259
“Create task”

12
00:00:31.259 --> 00:00:33.847
puts it in today’s agenda, never twice;

13
00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:36.912
nothing is sent or changed by itself.

14
00:00:38.012 --> 00:00:40.310
For each renewal you prepare terms:

15
00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:41.842
you see the last premium,

16
00:00:42.029 --> 00:00:44.582
enter the renewal premium and see the change.

17
00:00:44.885 --> 00:00:46.475
Then you record the decision:

18
00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:49.134
“Renewed”, “Client declined”

19
00:00:49.134 --> 00:00:50.887
or “Lapsed”.

20
00:00:51.987 --> 00:00:53.786
Nothing is renewed automatically:

21
00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.375
a renewal counts only when you record it.

22
00:00:56.561 --> 00:00:57.235
“Renewed”

23
00:00:57.235 --> 00:00:58.941
updates the premium from the renewal

24
00:00:58.941 --> 00:01:01.843
date and credits renewal production once.

25
00:01:02.943 --> 00:01:04.208
“General renewals”

26
00:01:04.208 --> 00:01:05.461
work as a pipeline:

27
00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:08.782
to start, quotes requested, compared,

28
00:01:08.806 --> 00:01:12.033
sent to client, approved, renewed or lost.

29
00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.400
Every move is a line on the client’s timeline.

30
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.379
Follow-ups are created on the days before expiry you

31
00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:23.012
set in Settings, for example forty-five, thirty and fifteen,

32
00:01:23.106 --> 00:01:26.263
or straight away with “Create follow-ups”.

33
00:01:27.363 --> 00:01:28.327
In the next lesson:

34
00:01:28.327 --> 00:01:30.810
insured items and overdue premiums.
